<title>USA: TABLE - Staffmark Inc Q2 net rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Staffmark Inc Q2 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>FAYETTEVILLE, Ark. 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>StaffMark, Inc.</p>
<p>			   Combined Statements of Income</p>
<p>		    (in thousands, expect per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    (Unaudited)</p>
<p>				 Three Months Ended  Six Months Ended</p>
<p>					   June 30,	 June 30,</p>
<p>			  1996 (a)	  1997  1996 (a)	 1997</p>
<p> Service revenues    $48,928     $96,123   $89,854   $159,987</p>
<p> Cost of Services     38,357	74,676    70,807    124,515</p>
<p> Gross Profit	   10,571	21,447    19,047     35,472</p>
<p>Operating Expenses:</p>
<p>Selling, general</p>
<p>  and administrative   7,258	14,074    14,197     24,006</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>  amortization	     491	 1,061	 919	1,749</p>
<p> Operating Income	2,822	 6,312     3,931	9,717</p>
<p>Pro Forma: (b)</p>
<p> Net Income		1,673	 3,452     2,067	5,667</p>
<p>Primary earnings per share</p>
<p>				0.18	  0.24	0.23	 0.39</p>
<p>Fully diluted</p>
<p>  earnings per share    0.18	  0.23	0.23	 0.38</p>
<p>NOTE: (a) Operating results for the three and six months ended June 30, 1996 will be reported to the Securities and Exchange Commission (&quot;SEC&quot;) in accordance with the provisions of the SEC Staff Accounting Bulletin No. 97. The pronouncement requires that one of the founding companies of StaffMark be identified as the acquirer for financial reporting purposes.</p>
<p>(b) Pro forma net income and earnings per share reflect the financial results of the operations of the companies which merged effective with the initial public offering.</p>
